[statement]
As `a-candidate-whose-dependency-cannot-be-met-is-passed-over-beside-one-depending-further-up`,
where a package up the chain of requirements was chosen for a name it only
provides: `top` needs `v`, which `p1` provides; `p1` needs `w`, which `p2`
and `p2b` provide, and `p2`, of the higher priority, is chosen for it;
`p2` needs `n`. `n` 2 needs `missing`, and `n` 1 needs `p1`; apk passes
over `n` 2 and installs `n` 1. The chain runs through `w`, the name `p2`
was chosen for, not `p2`, the name it carries. Where `p2` is the only
provider of `w`, apk refuses
(`a-candidate-whose-dependency-cannot-be-met-is-not-passed-over-beside-one-depending-further-up-through-single-providers`).

[repository]
P:top
V:1
D:v

P:p1
V:1
k:10
D:w
p:v

P:p2
V:1
k:10
D:n
p:w

P:p2b
V:1
p:w

P:n
V:2
D:missing

P:n
V:1
D:p1

[request]
top

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install n 1
install p2 1
install p1 1
install top 1
